{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"health has run out:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that despawn the same entity are safe."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn","anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns the real handles of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity with that handle.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Commands from Systems","anchor":"Commands-from-Systems"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded."}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Creating a Command Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"],"anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer"},{"title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"],"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer"},{"title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"],"anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities"},{"title":"Adding and Removing Components","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(_:into:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_:from:)"],"anchor":"Adding-and-Removing-Components"},{"title":"Changing the Hierarchy and Relations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/addChild(_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:childOf:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/removeParent(of:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/relate(_:_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/unrelate(_:_:fr